From: Folio <folio@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] @import and @font-face

RCSS has neither, so a stylesheet cannot pull in another one and a document cannot name the font
file it is designed around: faces have to be registered by the host before the document loads.

@import "file.rcss"; and @import url(file.rcss); parse the named stylesheet, resolved against the
importing one, in place: its rules come before anything after the @import in the cascade. Import
cycles are ignored with a warning, as is an @import inside @media.

@font-face takes font-family, src, font-style and font-weight, with src resolved against the
stylesheet. Faces are global to the library, so each family, style and weight is loaded once
however many stylesheets declare it, and a second declaration naming a different file is ignored
with a warning. A face the host registered first still wins its family. The file data is kept until
the font engine has shut down, since a face loaded from memory may keep pointing into it.

Removable once upstream supports @import and @font-face.

